Title:
MiMiNi-EDR (Windows Kernel-Mode EDR Agent)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
MiMiNi-EDR is a Windows kernel-mode + user-mode EDR prototype that monitors process/thread activity and applies basic detection and response actions in real time. The kernel driver registers process/thread creation callbacks and implements LSASS handle protection by stripping sensitive access rights when processes attempt to open LSASS. Events are queued in the driver and delivered to a user-mode agent via IRP/IOCTL communication, where simple rules flag common credential dumping and LSASS dumping patterns (e.g., mimikatz/sekurlsa, procdump, comsvcs.dll MiniDump abuse). The system can also enforce runtime “block rules” based on image name suffix and command-line substrings, and can terminate processes through the driver. It’s useful for defenders and security researchers learning Windows EDR design patterns, and for red teamers to understand common kernel/user telemetry and LSASS protection approaches. Interesting mainly as a compact reference implementation of callback-based monitoring + policy enforcement with a minimal rule engine.

Technical Focus:
- Kernel callbacks: PsSetCreateProcessNotifyRoutineEx / PsSetCreateThreadNotifyRoutine
- LSASS protection via ObRegisterCallbacks (handle access filtering)
- Kernel-to-user communication via IRP + IOCTL interface
- Command-line/process-name rule matching and process blocking
- Detection of LSASS dumping tradecraft (MiniDumpWriteDump, comsvcs.dll/rundll32 patterns)

Use Cases:
- Build a minimal EDR lab agent to study kernel telemetry and response flows
- Prototype LSASS handle protection and validate its impact on dump tooling
- Test simple behavioral/rule-based detections for credential dumping attempts
- Develop and evaluate user-mode rule engines driven by kernel event streams
- Create a controlled environment to measure attacker bypass attempts against callback-based monitoring

Keywords:
Windows kernel driver, EDR, PsSetCreateProcessNotifyRoutineEx, PsSetCreateThreadNotifyRoutine, ObRegisterCallbacks, LSASS, credential dumping, mimikatz, sekurlsa, MiniDumpWriteDump, comsvcs.dll, rundll32, procdump, IRP, IOCTL, process termination, handle access rights, PROCESS_VM_READ, PROCESS_QUERY_INFORMATION, WDK, test signing